---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import siteMeta from "../data/site-meta.json";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Home"
  description={siteMeta.description}
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-24 sm:py-32">
    <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">
      Tier 1 / 3 — Inline content
    </p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-3xl">
      This homepage is hardcoded in <code class="rounded bg-neutral-100 px-2 py-1 text-2xl">src/pages/index.astro</code>
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg text-neutral-500">
      There is no Markdown file behind it, no <code class="rounded bg-neutral-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-base">getEntry()</code> call,
      no content collection. Every word and section you see is written directly in the Astro file. Use this pattern for
      genuinely one-of-a-kind pages — landing pages, marketing pages, anything you only ever need one of.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
      <a href="/about" class="btn-primary">See the hybrid pattern →</a>
      <a href="/styleguide" class="btn-ghost">Style Guide</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The three tiers -->
  <section class="border-t border-neutral-200 bg-neutral-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-24 sm:py-32">
      <h2>Three content tiers, three working demos</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-neutral-500">
        Every page in this starter exists to demonstrate one of Astro's content patterns. Click through to see each one in action.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        <a href="/about" class="block rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 bg-white p-8 transition hover:border-neutral-400">
          <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">Tier 1 — Inline (hybrid variant)</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3">/about</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-neutral-500">
            The other shape of Tier 1: route file in <code class="rounded bg-neutral-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs">src/pages/about.astro</code> rendering a single
            Markdown entry from <code class="rounded bg-neutral-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs">src/content/pages/about.md</code>.
          </p>
        </a>

        <a href="/blog" class="block rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 bg-white p-8 transition hover:border-neutral-400">
          <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">Tier 2 — Posts collection</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3">/blog</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-neutral-500">
            Every card is a Markdown file in <code class="rounded bg-neutral-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs">src/content/posts/</code>.
            Schema in <code class="rounded bg-neutral-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs">src/content.config.ts</code>. Sorted by date.
          </p>
        </a>

        <a href="/projects" class="block rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 bg-white p-8 transition hover:border-neutral-400">
          <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">Tier 2 — Projects collection</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3">/projects</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-neutral-500">
            A different schema than posts — manual <code class="rounded bg-neutral-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs">order</code> field
            and a <code class="rounded bg-neutral-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs">featured</code> boolean. Demonstrates a non-chronological collection.
          </p>
        </a>

        <a href="/contact" class="block rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 bg-white p-8 transition hover:border-neutral-400">
          <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">Tier 3 — Site config driven</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3">/contact</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-neutral-500">
            The page imports <code class="rounded bg-neutral-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs">src/data/site-meta.json</code> and renders
            its values directly. The React contact form picks up the Formspree ID the same way.
          </p>
        </a>

        <div class="block rounded-xl border border-dashed border-neutral-300 p-8">
          <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">Tier 3 — More site config</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3">Nav &amp; Footer</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-neutral-500">
            The header and footer you see on every page also read from Tier 3 —
            <code class="rounded bg-neutral-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs">src/data/nav.json</code> and
            <code class="rounded bg-neutral-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs">src/data/footer.json</code>. Edit those files to update site-wide chrome.
          </p>
        </div>

        <a href="/styleguide" class="block rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 bg-white p-8 transition hover:border-neutral-400">
          <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">Design system</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3">/styleguide</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-neutral-500">
            A live preview of design tokens, typography, components. Backed by
            <code class="rounded bg-neutral-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs">src/styles/global.css</code> and
            <code class="rounded bg-neutral-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs">src/data/design-tokens.json</code>.
          </p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Decision rules -->
  <section class="border-t border-neutral-200">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-24 sm:py-32">
      <h2>Which tier should I use?</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-neutral-500">
        The decision tree is short. When in doubt, start inline and promote to a collection the moment you have a second one.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-3">
        <div>
          <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">Tier 1 — Inline</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm font-medium">A genuinely unique page</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-neutral-500">
            Homepage, about, contact, a one-off landing page. Write it directly in
            <code class="rounded bg-neutral-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs">src/pages/*.astro</code>, or pair the route file with a single
            entry in <code class="rounded bg-neutral-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs">src/content/pages/</code> for Markdown editing.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">Tier 2 — Content collection</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm font-medium">Repeating items sharing a schema</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-neutral-500">
            Blog posts, projects, products, team bios, testimonials, case studies. Define a Zod schema and add files to
            <code class="rounded bg-neutral-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs">src/content/&lt;collection&gt;/</code>.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">Tier 3 — Site config</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm font-medium">Structural data, not content</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-neutral-500">
            Nav links, footer groups, social handles, pricing tiers, redirects. Put it in
            <code class="rounded bg-neutral-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs">src/data/*.json</code> and import the JSON in your route or component.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-12 text-sm text-neutral-500">
        Full architecture and editing workflow: <a href="https://github.com" class="underline">docs/content-collections.md</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Interactivity model — orthogonal axis -->
  <section class="border-t border-neutral-200 bg-neutral-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-24 sm:py-32">
      <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">
        A separate axis — not a fourth tier
      </p>
      <h2 class="mt-3">Interactivity: when to add JavaScript</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-neutral-500">
        The three tiers above answer <em>where the content lives</em>. Islands answer a different question:
        <em>does this part of the page need to run JavaScript in the browser?</em> The two are orthogonal —
        any page (collection entry, inline route, config-driven) can include an island when interactivity demands it.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-3">
        <a href="/islands" class="block rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 bg-white p-8 transition hover:border-neutral-400 lg:col-span-2">
          <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">Concept demo</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3">/islands</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-neutral-500">
            Live demos of <code class="rounded bg-neutral-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs">client:load</code>,
            <code class="rounded bg-neutral-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs">client:idle</code>,
            <code class="rounded bg-neutral-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs">client:visible</code>. React and vanilla-JS examples.
            Decision rules for when to reach for an island vs. plain <code class="rounded bg-neutral-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs">.astro</code>.
          </p>
        </a>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-dashed border-neutral-300 p-8">
          <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">Default</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3">Zero JS</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-neutral-500">
            Most components in this starter are <code class="rounded bg-neutral-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs">.astro</code> — they ship as static HTML
            with no client-side runtime. Keep it that way unless interactivity demands otherwise.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Lorem fill / visual weight -->
  <section class="border-t border-neutral-200">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-24 sm:py-32">
      <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2 items-start">
        <div>
          <h2>Replace this section</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-neutral-500">
            Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Sed do eiusmod tempor incididunt ut labore et dolore
            magna aliqua. Ut enim ad minim veniam, quis nostrud exercitation ullamco laboris nisi ut aliquip ex ea commodo
            consequat.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-neutral-500">
            Duis aute irure dolor in reprehenderit in voluptate velit esse cillum dolore eu fugiat nulla pariatur.
            Excepteur sint occaecat cupidatat non proident, sunt in culpa qui officia deserunt mollit anim id est laborum.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-neutral-500">
            <strong>How to remove this:</strong> open
            <code class="rounded bg-neutral-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs">src/pages/index.astro</code> and delete this section.
            The whole homepage is hardcoded — no Markdown to track down.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="aspect-4/3 overflow-hidden rounded-xl bg-neutral-200">
          <img
            src="/images/placeholders/landscape-4x3.svg"
            alt="Placeholder image rendered from public/images/placeholders/landscape-4x3.svg"
            class="h-full w-full object-cover"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
